return {
["05:00"]={"It was \003five in the morning\004. He entered the railway station, looked around, and, feeling sleepy, took shelter in a corner of the waiting room.","The Seven Madmen","Roberto Arlt"},
["05:01"]={"Just \003after five o’clock\004 on this chill September morning, the fishmonger’s cart, containing Kirsten and Emilia and such possessions as they have been able to assemble in the time allowed to them, is driven out of the gates of Rosenborg?","Music and Silence","Rose Tremain"},
["05:02"]={"It was \0035:02 a.m.\004, December 14. In another fifty-eight minutes he would set sail for America. He did not want to leave his bride; he did not want to go.","The Prize","Brenda Joyce"},
["05:03"]={"It was \0035:03 a.m.\004 It didn’t matter. She wasn’t going to get back to sleep. She threw off her covers and, swearing at herself, Caleb and Mr. Griffin, she headed into the shower.","Unhallowed Ground","Heather Graham"},
["05:04"]={"\0035:04 a.m.\004 on the substandard clock radio. Because why do people always say the day starts now? Really it starts in the middle of the night at a fraction of a second past midnight.","The Accidental","Ali Smith"},
["05:05"]={"The baby, a boy, is born at \003five past five\004 in the morning.","The Namesake","Jhumpa Lahiri"},
["05:06"]={"\0035:06 a.m.\004 I wake up strangely energized, my stomach growling. Upstairs, the overstocked fridge offers me its bounty of sympathy food.","This Is Where I Leave You","Jonathon Tropper"},
["05:07"]={"He blinked, turned over, and stared at the fluorescent green figures on his bedside clock: \0035:07\004. More than enough time to go over the opening lines in his mind before getting up.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:08"]={"Ambrose and I will marry at Fort McHenry at \0035:08\004 EDST this coming Saturday, Rosh Hashanah!","Letters","John Barth"},
["05:09"]={"“You’ll have one by the side of your bed in a few years’ time, so you wouldn’t even need to go into your office,” said Su Ling, letting her head fall back on the pillow when she saw \0035:09\004 flick up on the bedside clock.","Sons of Fortune","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:10"]={"I settled into a daily routine. Wake up at 4:40 am, shower, get on the train north by \003ten after five\004.","Bossypants","Tina Fey"},
["05:11"]={"Today was Tuesday, the fifteenth of August; the sun had risen at \003eleven minutes past five\004 this morning and would set at two minutes before seven this evening.","The Hot Rock","Donald E. Westlake"},
["05:13"]={"Wu said, “You shut down at \003five-thirteen\004 this morning, and when you started back up, you started with auxiliary power.”","Jurassic Park","Michael Crichton"},
["05:14"]={"The time was \0035:14 am\004, a very strange time indeed for the sheriff to have seen what he claimed he saw as he made his early-morning rounds, first patrolling back and forth along the deserted, snowbound streets of Kingdom City before extending his vigilance northward, along County Road.","Into the Web","Thomas H. Cook"},
["05:15"]={"Weird conversation with Brown, a tired & confused old man who’s been jerked out of bed at \0035:15\004.","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson"},
["05:16"]={"\0035:16\004 — Mank on phone to Secretary of State Brown: ‘Mr. Brown, we’re profoundly disturbed about this situation in the 21st. We can’t get a single result out of there.’","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson"},
["05:17"]={"After managing to get roughly three hours of sleep, Grant checked the time on his phone. \0035:17 AM\004.\nMore sleep is unlikely. Time for a morning run.","Lionhearts","Ray Keating"},
["05:18"]={"ABOARD TPA 545\n\0035:18 A.M.\004\nEmily Jansen sighed in relief. The long flight was nearing an end. Morning sunlight streamed through the windows of the airplane.","Airframe","Michael Crichton"},
["05:19"]={"Scott eased himself into the corner before once again checking the little sulphur dots on his watch. It was \0035:19\004. He and Hannah had been in the safe for an hour and seventeen minutes.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:20"]={"If she can keep her speed to seventy until she leaves the turnpike at midtown, and if she catches most of the traffic lights, she estimates she can be at her building by \003five-twenty\004.","If It Bleeds","Stephen King"},
["05:22"]={"Yes, she nodded. “I will take off in the dark, and be over Tuti airfield at sunrise. That’s at \00305:22 hours\004.”","The Leopard Hunts in Darkness","Wilbur Smith"},
["05:23"]={"Tock wagged his tail proudly, but Milo didn’t say a word, and to this day no one knows of the lost week but the few people who happened to be awake at \0035:23\004 on that very strange morning.","The Phantom Tollbooth","Norton Juster"},
["05:24"]={"If I could count precisely to sixty between two passing orange minutes on her digital clock, starting at 5:23 am and ending exactly as it melted into \0035:24\004, then when she woke she would love me and not say this had been a terrible mistake.","The Tragedy of Arthur","Arthur Phillips"},
["05:25"]={"George’s train home from New Street leaves at \0035:25\004. On the return journey, there are rarely schoolboys.","Arthur and George","Julian Barnes"},
["05:27"]={"She looked at her watch. It was \0035:27 am\004. Surely Gawain would already be here? Wouldn’t he be looking out for her, since there was no obvious way of getting inside?","New York Valentine","Carmen Reid"},
["05:29"]={"\003Shortly before five-thirty\004 Father Martin woke himself with a shriek of terror. He jerked up in bed and sat, rigid as a doll, staring wild-eyed into the darkness.","Death in Holy Orders","P.D. James"},
["05:30"]={"On the day they were going to kill him, Santiago Nasar got up at \003five-thirty\004 in the morning to wait for the boat the bishop was coming on.","Chronicle of a Death Foretold","Gabriel García Márquez"},
["05:32"]={"By \00305:32\004 the driver had come back from a corner shop with a six-pack of Coke, a bottle of Jack Daniels, some sachets of breakfast milk, an armfull of stale cakes and a carton of Zhongncmhai cigarettes. The doors slammed shut and the van moved off.","Rare Earth","Paul Mason"},
["05:33"]={"It was \003five thirty-three\004 when we left. Is it six o’clock now? Six thirty? And Mark’s still in his cage and I’m scared to drive very fast… what if we don’t get there in time?","Among the Brave","Margaret Peterson Haddix"},
["05:34"]={"I asked “What time is sunrise?”\nA second’s silence while the crestfallen Bush absorbed his rebuke, and then another voice answered: “\003Five-thirty-four\004, sir.”","The Commodore","C.S. Forester"},
["05:35"]={"The Senator woke at \0035:35\004 in a cold sweat—not that he had really slept for more than a few minutes at any one time. It had been an evil night, thunder and lightning and sirens.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:36"]={"She drank a bottle of Jack Daniels. When she woke at \00305:36\004 she had wiped the previous evening.","The Fowler Family Business","Jonathan Meades"},
["05:37"]={"Richard glanced at the clock on the microwave — \0035:37\004 — almost twelve hours, almost one half-day since he’d dialed 911.","This Book Will Save Your Life","A.M. Homes"},
["05:39"]={"George took his phone from the dressing table. “The nightmare beat the alarm by just over an hour,” he said. “It’s \003twenty-one minutes to six\004.”","The E Utopia Project","Kudakwashe Muzira"},
["05:40"]={"At \0035:40 a.m.\004, he threw back the duvet, swung his legs out of bed, and placed his feet firmly on the carpet.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:41"]={"It took Inigo until \0035:41\004 before he actually cornered the Count. In the billiard room. “Hello,” he was about to say. “My name name is Inigo Montoya; you killed my father; prepare to die.”","The Princess Bride","William Goldman"},
["05:42"]={"At \003eighteen minutes to six\004, they blew the wall, and even then, it was almost too late.","A Gentleman’s Game","Greg Rucka"},
["05:43"]={"\0035:43\004 — Mank on phone to ‘Mary’ in Washington; ‘It now appears quite clear that we’ll lead the state — without the 21st.’","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson"},
["05:44"]={"And what time, again, did the defendant actually say these words?\n“That would have been — you can see the time on the film tape on the frame where you’ve stopped it. \0030544 hours\004.”","Invasion of Privacy","Perri O’Shaughnessy"},
["05:45"]={"At \0035:45\004 the following morning, the General was standing outside George’s tent in full dress uniform, carrying a black leather attaché case.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:46"]={"Herbert could feel nothing. He wrote a legal-sounding phrase to the effect that the sentence had been carried out at \0035:46 am\004, adding, ‘without a snag’. The burial party had cursed him quietly as they’d hacked at the thick roots and tight soil.","A Whispered Name","William Brodrick"},
["05:48"]={"A Bacardi mirror with fogged glass hangs above the backbar next to a St. Pauli Girl clock, the clock’s hands frozen at \003twelve minutes to six\004.","Northwest Corner","John Burnham Schwartz"},
["05:49"]={"Towards morning he slept more deeply. Even so, the harsh incessant ring of the telephone woke him to instant consciousness. The illuminated dial of his travelling clock showed \0035:49 a.m.\004","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["05:50"]={"It was was \0035:50\004 when he staggered from the room, heading he knew not where or for how long, but hoping only that whoever had been guiding him lately would not desert him now.","The Princess Bride","William Goldman"},
["05:52"]={"At \0035:52 am\004 paramedics from the St. Petersburg Fire Department and SunStar Medic One ambulance service responded to a medical emergency call at 12201 Ninth Street North, St. Petersburg, apartment 2210.","Silent Witness","Mark Fuhrman"},
["05:53"]={"At \003five fifty-three\004, as a blood-red sun peeped over the horizon, a Verey pistol was fired and Charlie looked back to see the sky lit up behind him.","As the Crow Flies","Jeffrey Archer"},
["05:54"]={"This morning, the sun came up at \003six minutes to six\004. There was already heavy early-morning rush-hour traffic on the Majesta Bridge. Meyer was driving. Carella was riding shotgun.","Merely Hate","Ed McBain"},
["05:55"]={"Billy doesn’t drive to the parking garage. The parking garage is done. At \003five to six\004 he parks on Main Street a few blocks from the Gerard Tower. Plenty of curbside spaces at this hour and the sidewalk is deserted.","Billy Summers","Stephen King"},
["05:56"]={"The officer with the chipped nose went over to borrow the watch of General Feraud. They bent their heads over them for a time. “That’s it. At \003four minutes to six\004 by yours.”","A Set of Six","Joseph Conrad"},
["05:57"]={"She smiles a bit but the next breath comes out louder like a moan. At \00305:57\004 I say, “Ma, it’s nearly six,” so she gets up to make dinner but she doesn’t eat any.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["05:58"]={"Loud crashes came from the flat below at \0035:58\004 this morning, though she’d been clock-watching long before that.","The Woman Downstairs","Elisabeth Carpenter"},
["05:59"]={"The shades in the corner room on the southeast were the first to be raised. It was the old rector’s bedroom. He was reading his Bible \003before the clock had struck six\004.","The Hammer of God","Bo Giertz"},
